      "id": "claim_f5a5ee8943c046eca2f6f00c065ad23d",
      "statement": "Each make localstack-db run is disposable by design: it generates a fresh master password and, if an RDS instance already exists, deletes and recreates it because LocalStack does not apply master-password changes via modify-db-instance, so prior row data is discarded while schema is rebuilt via bootstrap and migrations.",
